# Build output. Cargo.lock is committed deliberately and is not ignored.
/target

# What the fetch writes into the data directory is not tracked.
#
# Whether the compilation may be redistributed inside this repository is the
# third entry of issue #1 and is open, and `docs/data-terms.md` reads the terms
# as unclear on exactly that with the conservative reading stated. So a clone
# gets the tables by running `cargo fetch-compilation` rather than by cloning
# them.
#
# The provenance records are ignored with the files they describe rather than
# tracked beside them. A tracked record whose file is untracked is refused by
# the gate in every fresh clone, which is the check working: a record and the
# numbers it is about travel together or not at all.
#
# This is written here rather than as `data/.gitignore` because the gate
# requires a provenance record for every file under `data/` and grants exactly
# one exception, by path. A second file there would need a record describing
# numbers it does not carry.
/data/*
!/data/README.md
